<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Both too little and too much rain delayed 1997/98 wheat sowing in different parts of Argentina's grain belt, the government's Agricultural Secretariat said in its weekly crop report Thursday.</p>
<p>While almost all of Cordoba province and the southern and central regions of Santa Fe are still locked in drought, the soil is waterlogged in Buenos Aires, especially in the western and central parts of the province.</p>
<p>Around the country, farmers had sown 30.2 percent of a total intended area of around 6.5 million hectares by June 27. At the same point last season, farmers had sown 53.8 percent of a larger intended area.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..............</p>
<p> Wheat     6,500  30.2  (53.8)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,926  100.0(100.0) 3,062.1   95.0  (92.1)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,648  100.0(100.0) 6,313.5   99.2  (98.3)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,048  100.0(100.0) 2,936.2  100.0  (100.0</p>
<p> Sorghum     802  100.0(100.0)   671.7   98.7  (95.4)</p>
<p> Cotton	956  100.0  (n/a)   776.5   87.6  (83.1)</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
